v2.0.0 rebuilt the Baccarat module as a local Python server application. v2.1.0-v2.4.0 added the Tie
bet and its own stake, the half-screen layout, PASS recording the table's result, and the OCR
groundwork. v2.5.x-v2.7.x built and proved the OCR tooling, calibration, the confidence gate and the
live loop. v2.8.0 was the milestone: the reader read the user's live casino display correctly and
found that a region containing the history grid and the balance row makes the model burn its whole
token budget. v2.8.1 refused whole-screen regions and explained a profile changed while running.
v2.8.2 made the OCR profile follow the session's provider and layout, and made Draw the region start
from a detected table position.

v2.8.3 fixes the drawing coordinate conversion, which divided by the server's scale factor and so
moved every drawn box up and to the left whenever CSS shrank the picture — which it always does. The
user had been drawing the table correctly; the module was saving the chat panel. The conversion is now
by proportion, exact at any window width, and the Pragmatic Half Width / Full Length profile is
pre-measured at 1220,840,437x135 for a 1920x1080 screen so that layout needs no calibration at all.

The per-release record for the module is BACARAT/CHANGELOG.md.
